{"Successful cleanup batches now call r.log.Error and include the full ID list, which can generate repeated error-level logs with thousands of IDs every minute, triggering false error alerts and hiding real cleanup failures": 0.9843232035636902, "When a non-SQLite database is configured with a cleanup batch size above its parameter limit, the code creates one SQL parameter per annotation ID, which can cause the cleanup delete to fail before removing any rows": 0.9220242500305176, "The MaxCount cleanup path fetches excess IDs with OFFSET and deletes them in a separate statement, but if newer annotations are deleted between those statements, the stale ID list can cause more annotations to be removed than the configured max-count policy requires": 0.8281364440917969}